                <pb facs="0320" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/407: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in El Salvador</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McCafferty</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-25T15:00:00-06:00">January 25, 1934—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. The Foreign Office informed me that the Governments of Guatemala, Honduras,
                    and Nicaragua have recognized the present regime in Salvador today. The
                    recognitions were granted by telegrams from the Foreign Ministers of those
                    countries to the Salvadoran Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McCafferty</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
